// GDTF terrain tile-role table — DATA-DRIVEN atlas indices for the GTW-48 top-down
// battlefield draw (S4 / GTW-218). Maps each terrain ROLE to a TileIndex into
// assets/sprites/alt_tileset_terrain.png (16x22 = 352 tiles; index = row*16 + col,
// 0-based row-major). Edit freely — every field is a tunable index, hot-swappable
// through the same RonAsset<T> loader the theme / situation / tuning use; nothing
// about the index choices is hardcoded in Rust. Indices eyeballed against
// /tmp/terrain_labeled.png and confirmed before locking (DOOR + prop alts were
// [UNVERIFIED] in the draft; DOOR 339 reads as a dark hatch/doorway panel, locked).
(
    floor:           6,     // default walkable ground — brighter grey plating (GTW-373: 144 read too dark, 6 is brighter)
    floor_alt_panel: 128,    // alt floor — bolted/riveted grey panel (future variety, matches floor 6's palette)
    wall:            0,     // TerrainKind::Wall — heavy dark wall strip, NS orientation (GTW-373: re-tiled 16 -> 0, blocking geometry)
    wall_ew:         16,    // GTW-469 EW-orientation wall — row 0 col 0 (the NS `wall` at index 0) rotated 90deg into row 1 col 0 (index 16). Reproducible transform (ImageMagick): `magick alt_tileset_terrain.png -crop 16x16+0+0 +repage -background none -rotate 90 ew_wall.png` then `magick alt_tileset_terrain.png ew_wall.png -geometry +0+16 -composite alt_tileset_terrain.png`. Sim semantics identical to `wall` (Wall, LOS/move blocking); orientation is presentation-only.
    cover:           248,   // TerrainKind::Cover — chest-high crate/box cover prop on a floor cell
    slab:            22,    // SurfaceGrid Present slab — raised light-grey elevated deck panel
    rubble:          295,   // CoverDestroyed / damaged — sparse broken-debris scatter
    slab_destroyed:  295,   // SlabDestroyed treatment (GTW-367 C3, engineer's choice) — reuses the rubble broken-debris scatter so a collapsed deck reads as rubble (a swap, never a hole). ART-REVIEW: placeholder; a destroyed slab may want a DISTINCT tile (a hole punched to the level below / cracked deck) — re-point this index when art authors one
    door:            339,   // doorway / hatch panel — dark hatch tile (authored for future variety)
    stair_up:        29,    // VerticalLink Stair endpoint where you ASCEND (active storey is the link's LOWER cell). GTW-373 (user 2026-06-23) SUPERSEDES the GTW-359 OQ-3 single-stair:77 constant: the stair role is split into up/down, chosen by link direction
    stair_down:      28,    // VerticalLink Stair endpoint where you DESCEND (active storey is the link's UPPER cell). GTW-373 (user 2026-06-23) SUPERSEDES the GTW-359 OQ-3 single-stair:77 constant: the stair role is split into up/down, chosen by link direction
    ladder:          235,   // VerticalLink Ladder endpoint — ladder tile (UNCHANGED system constant, user OQ-3 ruling GTW-359)
    // GTW-470 ORIENTATION/DIRECTION door + stair tiles — each a DISTINCT AUTHORED tile the author
    // places explicitly in a prefab (orientation/direction is never presenter-inferred). The 6 new
    // indices were authored into previously-unused row-21 cells (cols 4..9, indices 340..345) by a
    // DETERMINISTIC, REPRODUCIBLE transform recorded below. PLACEHOLDER ART (derived/rotated from the
    // existing generic door 339 + stair 29/28 tiles) — flagged refinable; the user authors final art.
    //
    // Reproducible derivation (ImageMagick `magick`, sheet = assets/sprites/alt_tileset_terrain.png):
    //   door_ns  (340) = door  base 339 (col3,row21,x48,y336) as-is (the NS-running hatch).
    //   door_ew  (341) = door  base 339 rotated 90deg: `magick SHEET -crop 16x16+48+336 +repage -background none -rotate 90 door_ew.png`.
    //   stair_ns_up   (342) = stair_up   base 29 (col13,row1,x208,y16) as-is.
    //   stair_ns_down (343) = stair_down base 28 (col12,row1,x192,y16) as-is (up vs down are the two
    //                          DISTINCT existing stair tiles, not a pure rotation — ticket OQ (b)).
    //   stair_ew_up   (344) = stair_up   base 29 rotated 90deg.
    //   stair_ew_down (345) = stair_down base 28 rotated 90deg.
    //   Each target cell (340..345) was first cleared to transparent (Copy of a 16x16 xc:none patch)
    //   then the derived tile composited Over it, then `cp` over the asset (dims preserved 256x352).
    // Sim semantics: doors are sim_kind=Wall+Openable (block like a wall when closed; functional
    // open/close is GTW-315); stairs are sim_kind=Slab (walkable; vertical traversal is GTW-388).
    door_ns:         340,   // GTW-470 NS-orientation door (the dark hatch, NS-running)
    door_ew:         341,   // GTW-470 EW-orientation door (the NS hatch rotated 90deg)
    stair_ns_up:     342,   // GTW-470 NS-orientation stair you ASCEND (derived from stair_up 29)
    stair_ns_down:   343,   // GTW-470 NS-orientation stair you DESCEND (derived from stair_down 28)
    stair_ew_up:     344,   // GTW-470 EW-orientation stair you ASCEND (NS up rotated 90deg)
    stair_ew_down:   345,   // GTW-470 EW-orientation stair you DESCEND (NS down rotated 90deg)
)
